{
  "id": "rejected-ops",
  "title": "Ops the server refuses",
  "covers": [
    "ticket follow-up 7: rejected ops",
    "push: one rejected op does not block the rest of the batch",
    "clock: ops more than 24 h ahead of the server, or implausibly old reviews, are rejected"
  ],
  "narrative": [
    "B pushes ten ops in one batch and four more later. Thirteen are refused, each for its own reason (see `rejected`); none of them enters the log or changes any row.",
    "The tenth (card.flag_set, T+29) is accepted: a rejection never blocks later ops.",
    "The four clock rejections (SYNC.md 3.4) come from a phone whose date was wrong: two ahead (clock_ahead), one reset to 1970 and one before the card existed (clock_behind). They can only be discarded (SYNC.md 10.4).",
    "On B the thirteen pending_op rows become state 'rejected' with last_error = '<code>: <message>'; their local effects stay until the user discards them (SYNC.md section 10)."
  ],
